          <mxGeometry height="130" width="280" x="450" y="4890" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-tMHPxVwaKHQxEQfK2Ct-10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=19;" value="Weights:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Weights are the learnable numbers inside the model that determine how inputs are transformed into outputs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Weight tying scheme:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Weight tying is a technique where the input embedding matrix and output prediction layer share the same weights to reduce parameters and improve language modeling.&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="640" x="90" y="5090" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-tMHPxVwaKHQxEQfK2Ct-11" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=14;" value="&lt;h1 data-start=&quot;514&quot; data-end=&quot;548&quot;&gt;What Is the Residual Stream?&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;550&quot; data-end=&quot;667&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;In a Transformer, the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;572&quot; data-end=&quot;591&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;residual stream&lt;/strong&gt; is the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;599&quot; data-end=&quot;666&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;main vector representation that flows through the whole neural network&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;669&quot; data-end=&quot;681&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Every block:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol data-start=&quot;683&quot; data-end=&quot;748&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;683&quot; data-end=&quot;701&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;686&quot; data-end=&quot;701&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Reads from it&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;702&quot; data-end=&quot;718&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;705&quot; data-end=&quot;718&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Modifies it&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;719&quot; data-end=&quot;748&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;722&quot; data-end=&quot;748&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Adds its update back to it&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;750&quot; data-end=&quot;830&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;So the residual stream is like the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;785&quot; data-end=&quot;829&quot;&gt;central information highway of the model&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;750&quot; data-end=&quot;830&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;750&quot; data-end=&quot;830&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Activation - These are functions that keep the neural network to be in multi layer not a single linear layer like other models. For eg: GELU used in gpt model&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="280" width="694" x="76" y="5380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="EkmF1OC7JyBp3kpmVwTX-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=14;" value="In float datatype there are 3 parts:&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Sign | Exponent | Mantissa&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;754&quot; data-end=&quot;807&quot;&gt;Floating numbers are stored like scientific notation:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex-display&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex-mathml&quot;&gt;&lt;math xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&quot; display=&quot;block&quot;&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;v&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;a&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;l&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;u&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;(&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mo&gt;−&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mo stretchy=&quot;false&quot;&gt;)&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;s&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;g&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo&gt;×&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;1.&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mi&gt;m&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;a&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;t&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;i&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;s&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;s&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;a&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;×&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;x&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;p&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;o&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;e&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;t&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;value = (-1)^{sign} \times 1.mantissa \times 2^{exponent}&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex-display&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1040&quot; data-end=&quot;1146&quot;&gt;The &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1044&quot; data-end=&quot;1056&quot;&gt;mantissa&lt;/strong&gt; (also called &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1070&quot; data-end=&quot;1082&quot;&gt;fraction&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1086&quot; data-end=&quot;1101&quot;&gt;significand&lt;/strong&gt;) stores the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1114&quot; data-end=&quot;1145&quot;&gt;actual digits of the number&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1148&quot; data-end=&quot;1180&quot;&gt;It determines the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1166&quot; data-end=&quot;1179&quot;&gt;precision&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1148&quot; data-end=&quot;1180&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1182&quot; data-end=&quot;1190&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;1192&quot; data-end=&quot;1213&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;1.101011 × 2³&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1215&quot; data-end=&quot;1220&quot;&gt;Here:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;1222&quot; data-end=&quot;1249&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;1.101011 → mantissa&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1251&quot; data-end=&quot;1314&quot;&gt;The more bits in the mantissa, the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1286&quot; data-end=&quot;1313&quot;&gt;more precise the number&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1251&quot; data-end=&quot;1314&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1251&quot; data-end=&quot;1314&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Different floating-point formats trade &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;1587&quot; data-end=&quot;1610&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;precision vs memory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Format&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Bits&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Mantissa&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Exponent&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;FP32&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;32&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;23&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;FP16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;BF16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex-display&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex&quot;&gt;Here for creation of gpt2 model we will be using BF32 datatype because of large dynamic range like FP32 but the mantissa part is smaller which makes training more stable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex-display&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;katex&quot;&gt;since mantissa is decreased, so precision also get reduced. But the range is same as f32. In neural network precision doesn&#39;t hurt much but if we get wide range of numbers then the model learns more and the training is good.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="580" width="972.5" x="77.5" y="5800" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="IIMvIxR4qmjR_G1lhBKG-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=17;" value="torch.compile(model):&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;Its like GCC in C or C++. It works like a compiler. In pytorch it provides this functionality. Python generally uses interpreter and so it computes each and every step 1 by 1, for which it becomes slow when there is a huge computation to carry on.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;For eg: In GELU activation function if we do not use compile then it will take each an every element one by one add to each operations of the function one by 1, but compile takes all the elements at once from the memory and does the full calculation at 1 go in GPU and GPU sends back the output to the memory in 1 go, for which computations speeds up when training or running with large data and having multiple functions.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="600" x="90" y="6480" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KvEF-lHIjNREQJ-d6xup-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=15;" value="&lt;b&gt;Flash attention:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;This is a computation technique generally used in transformer part of a gpt model, which&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;makes attention &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;125&quot; data-end=&quot;166&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;much faster and more memory efficient.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;125&quot; data-end=&quot;166&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In normal attention memory grows like O(T&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;)&amp;nbsp; while in flash attention it grows in O(T).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;699&quot; data-end=&quot;817&quot;&gt;Flash Attention is an &lt;strong data-start=&quot;721&quot; data-end=&quot;816&quot;&gt;optimized algorithm for computing attention without storing the full T × T matrix in memory&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;819&quot; data-end=&quot;830&quot;&gt;Instead it:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;832&quot; data-end=&quot;949&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full mt-4 mb-1&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Processes attention in small blocks&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Keeps values in fast GPU SRAM&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Avoids writing large matrices to GPU memory&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;951&quot; data-end=&quot;981&quot;&gt;So it reduces memory movement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;951&quot; data-end=&quot;981&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;951&quot; data-end=&quot;981&quot;&gt;There is a 1 drawback with flash attention and pytorch.compile integration that&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Flash Attention may not appear explicitly in the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-start=&quot;3065&quot; data-end=&quot;3082&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;torch.compile()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; graph because it runs as a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;3110&quot; data-end=&quot;3139&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;special fused CUDA kernel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, but it can still be used internally if attention is implemented through &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code data-start=&quot;3213&quot; data-end=&quot;3245&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;scaled_dot_product_attention()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="270" width="1120" x="77.5" y="6840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
